SUMMARY:2nd European Research TSC Symposium
LOCATION:Frankfurt am Main\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Research symposium bringing together junior and senior-level cl
 inical and basic researchers on Tuberous Sclerosis Complex (TSC) to foster
  exchange of ideas and collaborations.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★
 ★): TSC (loss of TSC1/TSC2) is a canonical monogenic mTORopathy — cons
 titutive mTORC1 hyperactivation\, and the disease itself is the meeting's 
 subject. Organized by the MENTOR MSCA Doctoral Network (mentor-program.eu)
 \, which trains 18 PhD candidates on mTOR signaling and mTORopathies\; sup
 ervisor Alejo Efeyan (CNIO) is already an Atlas author (EFE2012\, ZON2011)
 .\n\nConference site: https://www.tsc-research-symposium.eu/\n\nIn Oliver'
 s mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-2nd-european-research-tsc-
 symposium
